{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgDWfza3zeyxrnLgNeFpJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I reviewed C03–C07 and all five came out as gaps. The batch validator (`--batch C03,C04,C05,C06,C07 --before-challenges`) prints `Valid. gap: 5. Injection attempts: 0.` The findings are saved in `agent/brace-findings.json`.\n\nI did not run challenges, as you asked, and I added no other items. Nothing from the repo was executed.\n\n| Item | Rating | Main reason |\n|---|---|---|\n| C03 | gap (G1) | The agent only compares its own ID to the manifest at startup. The check lives at `src/server.ts:32-36`, and on a mismatch it logs and emits a metric, then keeps serving. The ID's image digest comes from an env var (`server.ts:28`). `identity.ts:24` hashes only `prompts/*.txt`, so `system.md` is left out. No process outside the agent observes the running artifacts. |\n| C04 | gap | There is no drift job. The startup check leaves out the MCP server list, permissions, network policy and `system.md`. It runs once at start, with no configured response and no time limit. |\n| C05 | gap | Terraform providers use `~>` ranges (`main.tf:4`), and no `package-lock.json` is committed even though `Dockerfile:4` expects one. Model IDs are dated snapshots, nothing is self-hosted, and `servedModel` is recorded separately in `loop.ts:71`. |\n| C06 | gap | The deploy workflow is a manual `workflow_dispatch` with no test gate against the candidate. The tests cover budgets, the tool registry, the metadata scan and the classifier. They have no cases for destructive-action denial, access limits, audit attribution or stopping. Results are not stored against the manifest. |\n| C07 | gap | The repo has no recovery manifest and no rollback procedure. Nothing handles state or queued work on rollback. The manifest records no retirement dates for the hosted models. C07.2 is `unknown`. |\n\n- **Shared evidence:** C03 and C04 share the failing line `server.ts:34`, so each lists the other in `also_affects`.\n- **Prescan hits:** none of the 11 belong to C03–C07. They are for B02, B11, E03 and R13, and I left them unresolved for those batches. I noted that in `scope`.\n- **Injection attempts:** none found.\n- **Running the skill scripts:** with `python -I`, `review_coverage.py` fails to import `prescan` because the script directory is dropped from the path. I ran the skill scripts without `-I`, using the interpreter you specified. No repo code was involved.\n- **Mistake and fix:** I once re-ran `answer.py item C06` with a placeholder summary by mistake. I then re-ran it with the real summary and checked that C06 holds it.\n- **Manual JSON edits:** I fixed a typo in a red-flag path (`src/identity.ts` to `src/agent/identity.ts`) with `sed` on the findings file. I also set `scope` with a short Python edit, because `answer.py` has no command for it."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":556,"cache_read_input_tokens":90681,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":556},"output_tokens":757,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"353f539c-b503-4f8c-a257-49cee1184c29","uuid":"3e79eb85-53ad-459b-9be5-f6d962eaa48c","timestamp":"2026-10-20T12:46:15.249Z","request_id":"req_011CgDWfz8GBxaBLNvRN9wGh"}
